.TH CTBREC-AUTO-PORTRAITS-REMOTE 1 "2026-11-09" "ctbrec-auto-portraits-remote" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ctbrec-auto-portraits-remote \- run ctbrec-auto-portraits in the ctbrec container over ssh
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ctbrec-auto-portraits-remote
[\fIOPTIONS\fP]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ctbrec-auto-portraits-remote
is a thin local wrapper that executes
.B /usr/local/bin/ctbrec-auto-portraits
inside the ctbrec Proxmox container (VMID 109 by default) as the
.B ctbrec
user, with
.B HOME=/home/ctbrec
so that config and state paths resolve identically to the running server.
.P
It connects with
.BR ssh (1)
in non-interactive mode (no TTY, host
.B RemoteCommand
disabled, batch mode) and then uses
.BR pct (1)
to enter the container. All argument parsing, HTTP requests and portrait
writes happen on the server; only the progress output is streamed back.
.P
Arguments are shell-quoted on the way through, so values containing spaces are
safe. The remote exit status becomes the wrapper's exit status.
.SH OPTIONS
All options are forwarded verbatim to
.BR ctbrec-auto-portraits (1).
The most useful are
.BR \-\-dry\-run ,
.BR \-\-limit ,
.BR \-\-normalize ,
.BR \-\-force
and
.BR \-\-quiet ;
see that page for the full list.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CTBREC_AUTO_PORTRAITS_SERVER
SSH host to run on. Defaults to
.BR proxmox .
.TP
.B CTBREC_AUTO_PORTRAITS_VMID
Proxmox container ID. Defaults to
.BR 109 .
.TP
.B CTBREC_AUTO_PORTRAITS_BIN
Path to the remote executable. Defaults to
.BR /usr/local/bin/ctbrec-auto-portraits .
.SH EXAMPLES
Preview the backfill plan:
.IP
.EX
ctbrec-auto-portraits-remote \-\-dry\-run
.EE
.P
Fetch at most 25 portraits now:
.IP
.EX
ctbrec-auto-portraits-remote \-\-limit 25
.EE
.P
Convert existing webp portraits to JPEG:
.IP
.EX
ctbrec-auto-portraits-remote \-\-normalize
.EE
.P
Re-fetch every recorded model:
.IP
.EX
ctbrec-auto-portraits-remote \-\-force \-\-quiet
.EE
.SH EXIT STATUS
The exit status of the remote
.BR ctbrec-auto-portraits (1).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ctbrec-auto-portraits (1),
.BR ctbrec-webui-patch (1),
.BR ssh (1),
.BR pct (1)
